  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Melphalan is an alkylating anticancer drug used mainly to treat multiple myeloma, and also other cancers such as ovarian and breast cancer and childhood tumours like neuroblastoma. It is an approved medicine, authorised in the European Union, and is also used in conditioning before stem cell transplantation.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2298283&quot;>Wikidata Q2298283</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>melphalan</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L01AA03</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01042&quot;>DB01042</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/460612&quot;>460612</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:28876&quot;>28876</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2298283&quot;>Q2298283</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C13H18Cl2N2O2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>305.199 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
